  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ parameter names without types
  |
  = note: C99 §6.7.5.3p3: an identifier list in a function declarator that is not part of a definition shall be empty

sema-permerrors-permissive.c:7:21: warning: 'return' with no value, in function returning non-void [-Wreturn-mismatch]
  |
7 | int nothing(void) { return; }
  |                     ^^^^^^^ no return value
  |
  = note: C99 §6.8.6.4p1: a return statement without an expression shall only appear in a function returning void; C89 permitted it

sema-permerrors-permissive.c:8:27: warning: 'return' with a value, in function returning void [-Wreturn-mismatch]
  |
8 | void value(void) { return 1; }
  |                           ^ value returned from a void function
  |
  = note: C99 §6.8.6.4p1: a return statement with an expression shall not appear in a function returning void

